 Export `start(api)` to receive `{ app, webContents, mainWindow, dshHome }`; `mainWindow()` returns the current primary window or `undefined`. Return a synchronous cleanup function or an object with `dispose()` to clean up on `will-quit`. Each extension's discovery, startup, and cleanup errors are logged with its package name without blocking other extensions. Restart Desktop after installing or changing extensions; hot reload is not supported. The Host environment advertises this capability as `DSH_DESKTOP_MAIN_EXTENSIONS=1`.
 
+### Native browser views
+
+`dshDesktop.browser.nativeViews` protocol 1 owns sandboxed WebContentsViews in the primary window. `acquire(scope, workspace)` requires a canonical tab address admitted by Sidebar-right; `attach(lease, slot)` composes the view in that slot. `command`, `onState` and idempotent `release` remain lease-scoped. A document is ready only after attachment and a committed generation with frame and loader ids. Owner reload, slot revocation and guest failure destroy the view. Unsupported commands are refused before CDP dispatch. Trusted main extensions receive `browserGuests` with scoped `snapshot`, `command`, `fetch` and `release`, not an authority-bearing numeric WebContents id.
+
 ### Startup onboarding
 
 The API-key input starts empty and uses `autocomplete="new-password"` to ask Chromium not to autofill saved login passwords.
